[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819810820","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105632#issuecomment-2819810820","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105632","id":2819810820,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oEuYE","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T01:11:28Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T01:11:28Z","body":"> Should it be named something like deep_equals to make its purpose clearer?\r\n\r\nYeah. I always assume shallow comparison unless explicitly specified otherwise\r\n\r\nThis PR doesn't account for cyclic dependencies so I think this will crash:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar a = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2}\r\nvar b = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2}\r\na[\"ref\"] = b\r\nb[\"ref\"] = a\r\nprint(is_equal(a, b))\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819810820/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821002629","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105632#issuecomment-2821002629","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105632","id":2821002629,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oJRWF","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T11:18:45Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T11:20:20Z","body":"Should this just use `Variant::identity_compare` or `Variant::hash_compare`, outside of `Object`?\r\n\r\nAlso this needs a recursion limit I'd say","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821002629/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821063961","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105632#issuecomment-2821063961","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105632","id":2821063961,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oJgUZ","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T11:43:53Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T11:43:53Z","body":"It should probably be called `deep_equals` to make its purpose much clearer. Otherwise at a glance it looks like a more complex `==` operator. A bit iffy on naming it after \"equality\" too, because it's actually checking for \"equivalence\", but Godot is also no stranger to mixing the terms up. Unsure...","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821063961/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821095095","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105632#issuecomment-2821095095","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105632","id":2821095095,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oJn63","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T11:57:03Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T11:57:03Z","body":"Also, most notably, there's a few similar methods. Adding one more may make things more confusing, due of the small intricacies of each one. But again, it's a few.\r\nNamely, Dictionary already has `recursive_equal`. Although, one may consider deprecating it in favour of the all-encompassing function this PR provides? Or just letting both coexist and share the same behaviour, or making the difference clearer.\r\nthe global scope's `is_same` comes to mind, as well.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821095095/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821148236","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105632#issuecomment-2821148236","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105632","id":2821148236,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oJ05M","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T12:18:00Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T12:18:00Z","body":"> > Should it be named something like deep_equals to make its purpose clearer?\n> \n> \n> \n> Yeah. I always assume shallow comparison unless explicitly specified otherwise\n> \n> \n> \n> This PR doesn't account for cyclic dependencies so I think this will crash:\n> \n> \n> \n> ```gdscript\n> \n> var a = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2}\n> \n> var b = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2}\n> \n> a[\"ref\"] = b\n> \n> b[\"ref\"] = a\n> \n> print(is_equal(a, b))\n> \n> ```\n\nThis could be solved with https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11919 / see linked issues.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821148236/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821226231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105632#issuecomment-2821226231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105632","id":2821226231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oKH73","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T12:48:42Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T12:48:42Z","body":"> This could be solved with https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11919 / see linked issues\r\n\r\nAre you sure it's related? Your proposal says `Dictionary could be made copy-on-write, the same way that Array is.` but this PR crashes with Array as well:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar a = [1]\r\nvar b = [1]\r\na.append(b)\r\nb.append(a)\r\nprint(is_equal(a, b))\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt can also compare Objects and they can also have cyclic references in their properties so it needs to keep track of what's been visited to prevent infinite recursion (or accept max depth as an argument), correct me if I'm wrong","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821226231/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821973026","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105632#issuecomment-2821973026","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105632","id":2821973026,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oM-Qi","user":{"login":"Geometror","id":50084500,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDg0NTAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50084500?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror","html_url":"https://github.com/Geometror","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-22T17:12:26Z","updated_at":"2025-04-22T17:24:02Z","body":"Regarding the cyclic references problem: I would go for the simplest solution in this case and use a maximum comparison depth of ~~128~~*, in addition to maybe printing a warning.\r\nOf course there are more sophisticated solutions, however, you pay the cost for those even when comparing non-cyclic stuff, which is the common case I'd argue.\r\n\r\n\\* EDIT: There's this in typedefs.h:\r\n```cpp\r\n// Limit the depth of recursive algorithms when dealing with Array/Dictionary\r\n#define MAX_RECURSION 100\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2821973026/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2829151918","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105632#issuecomment-2829151918","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105632","id":2829151918,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ooW6u","user":{"login":"Geometror","id":50084500,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDg0NTAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50084500?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror","html_url":"https://github.com/Geometror","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T00:58:16Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T00:58:16Z","body":"Renamed to `deep_equals` and added the recursion depth limit.\r\n\r\nJust for reference:\r\n## `is_same`\r\n\"Returns `true`, for value types, if `a` and `b` share the same value. Returns `true`, for reference types, if the references of `a` and `b` are the same.\" (quoted from docs)\r\n(`is_same` uses the `==` operator for `Object`s, so they are compared by object ID)\r\n\r\n## `==` and `recursive_equal`\r\n- the `==` operator uses `Variant::hash_compare` which calls `recursive_equal` (only exposed for `Dictionary`) on `Array` and `Dictionary`, whereby `Object`s are compared by reference (object ID)\r\n- Changing the behavior of `==` for `Object`s would be a massive compat-breakage (so we can't just modify `Variant::hash_compare`)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2829151918/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2830315755","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105632#issuecomment-2830315755","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105632","id":2830315755,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oszDr","user":{"login":"Geometror","id":50084500,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDg0NTAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50084500?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror","html_url":"https://github.com/Geometror","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T12:38:16Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T12:38:16Z","body":"@AThousandShips \r\n> Should this just use Variant::identity_compare or Variant::hash_compare, outside of Object?\r\n\r\nVariant types other than `Array`, `Dictionary` and `Object` use `==` which calls `Variant::hash_compare`. However, using `==`/`Variant::hash_compare` also for arrays and dictionaries breaks when they contain objects.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2830315755/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]